subproblem.statement:
Let P, n, ℓ ∈ ℕ and let U ⊆ ℝ^P be any set. Let T_r ∈ D_n(U) (r ∈ ℕ), T ∈ D_n(U), R_r ∈ D_{n+1}(U) (r ∈ ℕ), S_r ∈ D_n(U) (r ∈ ℕ), X ∈ D_{n+1}(U) and Y ∈ D_n(U). Assume:
(a) T_r(ω) − T_{r+1}(ω) = ∂R_r(ω) + S_r(ω) for all r ∈ ℕ and all ω ∈ D^n(U);
(b) T_r ⇀ T, i.e. T_r(ω) → T(ω) as r → ∞ for every ω ∈ D^n(U);
(c) for every η ∈ D^{n+1}(U) the real series Σ_{k∈ℕ} R_{ℓ+k}(η) has sum X(η) (HasSum);
(d) for every ω ∈ D^n(U) the real series Σ_{k∈ℕ} S_{ℓ+k}(ω) has sum Y(ω) (HasSum).
Then T_ℓ(ω) − T(ω) = ∂X(ω) + Y(ω) for every ω ∈ D^n(U).
